// CF-2: an unconditional discard is not a special encoding.
//
// The reference MATERIALISES a true condition - a MOV of the literal 1.0
// into the condition register with cc_update - and then uses the same
// KIL (NE.x) as every guarded discard.  There is exactly one KIL
// spelling.  (The old design note guessed "KIL with condition TR"; it was
// written before anyone compiled one.)
//
// Instructions before the discard are still emitted: the store of `c` to
// the colour register is there even though nothing survives to read it.
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    discard;
    o = c;
}
